compare this equation to general equation i.e. $\frac{\mathrm{dx}}{\mathrm{dy}}+\mathrm{Px}=\mathrm{Q} \Rightarrow \mathrm{P}=\frac{1}{\mathrm{y}}, \mathrm{Q}=\mathrm{y}^{2}\begin{array}{l}
\therefore \text { I.f. }=\mathrm{e}^{\int \mathrm{Pdy}}=\mathrm{e}^{\int \frac{1}{y} \mathrm{dy}}=\mathrm{e}^{\log y}=\mathrm{y} \\
\mathrm{x} \times \mathrm{I} \mathrm{f} .=\int \mathrm{Q} \times \text { I.f.dy }+\mathrm{C}_{1} \\
\Rightarrow \mathrm{x} \cdot \mathrm{y}=\int \mathrm{y}^{2} \cdot \mathrm{y} \mathrm{dy}+\mathrm{C}_{1} \Rightarrow \mathrm{xy}=\frac{\mathrm{y}^{4}}{4}+\mathrm{C}_{1} \\
\Rightarrow 4 \mathrm{xy}=\mathrm{y}^{4}+4 \mathrm{C}_{1} \\
\Rightarrow \mathrm{y}^{4}=4 \mathrm{xy}-4 \mathrm{C}_{1} \Rightarrow \mathrm{y}^{4}=4 \mathrm{xy}+\mathrm{C}
\end{array}
where $\mathrm{C}=-4 \mathrm{C}_{1}$

